^["implicit-roots"]{
  # Files that use default roots (@src, @docs, @examples, @spec) without declaring them locally.
  # This is valid, but making roots explicit improves portability and reduces ontology drift.
  !["Top implicit-root users (sample)"]
  .. @docs/audit-guide.spw  # uses implicit roots: src
  .. @src/platform/docs/audit-guide.spw  # uses implicit roots: src
  .. @src/runtime/docs/audit-guide.spw  # uses implicit roots: src
  .. @src/ui/docs/audit-guide.spw  # uses implicit roots: src
}

^["recommendations"]{
  1. Add ^["meta"] blocks to the core docs in docs/ (architecture, operators, patterns, etc).
  2. Prefer explicit roots (@here, @src) in each doc when the file has many cross-references.
  3. Use question blocks (?["…"]{ … }) as a standard navigation probe surface for each major doc.
  4. Keep index.spw files as "fruit": stable lists of links, minimal prose, consistent roots.
  5. Treat audits as pruning notes: link from docs/audits/index.spw and reference the affected files under ^["files"].
}

?["How does this surface orient the developer's attention or workflow?"]
  #:scope #!file
  ~#probe: "trace which claims or conventions reference this surface"

